cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DesiUtils ephemeris calibration"
message: "If you refer to these measurements, please cite this artifact."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A frozen calibration artifact for the DesiUtils browser ephemeris. Contains the harnesses, the
  retained JPL Horizons reference fetches and the regenerated outputs behind two defects found and
  fixed in the engine: UT-tagged Julian days passed to routines expecting dynamical-time JDE, and
  sidereal longitudes retaining nutation in longitude because a mean ayanamsa was subtracted from
  an apparent tropical longitude. The JPL Horizons legs and the nutation-in-longitude distribution
  are reproducible from this artifact. The Swiss Ephemeris confirmation matrix it also records is
  reviewer-reported and is not reproduced here.
authors:
  - name: "DesiUtils"
    website: "https://desiutils.in"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DesiUtils/ephemeris-calibration"
url: "https://desiutils.in/blog/kundli-calculator-accuracy"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - ephemeris
  - VSOP87
  - delta-T
  - nutation
  - sidereal
  - ayanamsa
  - calibration
  - reproducibility
